	'k041fc8ce' => 'Contact and visit',
	'k0590de96' => 'IN THEIR CASE',
	'k07b84f2a' => 'Our adult services are led by experienced clinicians dedicated to restoring communication dignity and vocal stamina. Therapist Mateo Lindqvist works with adult clients recovering from stroke, addressing aphasia and profound word-finding difficulties through dignified, real-world conversational strategies. Therapist Amara Osei supports teenagers and adults who stammer, guiding clients through speech modification techniques and building authentic speaking ease for presentations, interviews, and social interactions. Therapist Mina Castell specializes in vocal care and rehabilitation for occupational voice users, including teachers, singers, and professionals who speak all day, addressing chronic hoarseness and vocal fatigue. Our clinicians conduct unhurried forty-five-minute sessions, ensuring adult clients feel thoroughly respected, supported, and empowered to regain command of their voices in daily life.',
	'k080b7706' => 'Itemised receipts for your insurer. Please give 24 hours\' notice to cancel.',
	'k081dba56' => 'Rehearsed with notes in hand.',
	'k099d25ca' => '2F, 18 Linden Row, Westmere<br>Mon–Fri 08:30–18:30 · Sat 09:00–13:00<br>Closed Sun and public holidays',
	'k0ae8c3b5' => 'In the room',
	'k0bf8f67c' => 'First visit and fees',
	'k0c7b92cc' => 'minutes of home practice a day',
	'k0d377f86' => 'Here are answers to the questions families and adult clients most frequently ask about our speech therapy services, appointments, and fees. If you have a specific inquiry not covered here, Claire Dumont is always happy to assist.',
	'k0f67c4af' => 'Signs worth a call and what parents do in the room',
	'k0fc3d70e' => '2F, 18 Linden Row, Westmere',
	'k0fd6f1e1' => 'Our therapy follows a clear, unhurried rhythm designed around real conversation rather than mechanical drills. Through three connected stages—Listen, Practise, and Carry it home—we ensure communication skills flourish beyond our clinic walls.',
	'k108f4837' => 'Opening hours and appointment times',
	'k118ac223' => 'FIND US',
	'k11f3345e' => 'We stand by our waiting time promise: all new clients are seen for an assessment within two weeks of their first call with Claire Dumont. We understand that waiting months for a developmental evaluation causes immense stress for families and delays vital recovery for stroke survivors. By carefully managing our clinical diary and caseloads, we ensure prompt access to our therapists without placing clients on prolonged waiting lists.',
	'k1277e359' => 'Time to find',
	'k1350354c' => 'What should we do between weekly appointments?',
	'k13b9b76e' => 'Will my private health insurance cover therapy fees?',
	'k143da5ad' => 'What the first day looks like for children and adults',
	'k149dc62c' => 'Why forty-five minutes and one therapist',
	'k154d9bb4' => 'Animal cards on the mat.',
	'k1623afcc' => 'A free 15-minute phone conversation with the family coordinator to discuss what you notice and answer questions.',
	'k16941e54' => 'What to bring to your appointment',
	'k17ddc0b9' => '15 min',
	'k1c28b42c' => 'Once we understand your communication patterns, therapy moves into active practice. Each session lasts exactly forty-five minutes and is conducted by the same dedicated speech and language therapist every week. We do not rotate staff or leave clients working independently with software. Instead, the session is structured around dynamic games, tactile objects, mirror practice, or guided conversation tailored to the individual. We break complex communication hurdles into manageable steps, celebrating subtle milestones and adjusting techniques immediately when a task feels too easy or frustrating. Because you work with one clinician throughout your block of care, you never waste time establishing rapport or repeating your history. The entire forty-five minutes is dedicated to focused, supportive, and restorative practice.',
	'k1d5c5917' => 'Most clients achieve their best outcomes through structured therapy blocks. Booking a block of 8 sessions for €640 secures your designated therapist at the same weekly time slot, ensuring unbroken clinical momentum. For occupational voice users experiencing fatigue or hoarseness, our voice care course provides 6 sessions of 45 minutes for €480, addressing breath support, resonance, and vocal recovery. When therapy requires observing communication in authentic everyday environments, our therapists provide school or workplace visits for €120 per 60-minute session. These off-site consultations allow us to collaborate directly with classroom teachers or workplace colleagues, adapting desks, seating, and listening conditions to support practical communication success outside our clinic rooms.',
	'k1e4ffc13' => 'Adult rehabilitation, voice and stammering',
	'k1ef1eb09' => 'How we work',
	'k201e41a0' => 'Every therapy session at Hibiki Speech lasts forty-five minutes, which we have found to be the ideal duration for sustained concentration without exhaustion. Communication demands significant mental and emotional energy, particularly for a toddler exploring new sounds or an adult recovering after a stroke. Shorter sessions often end just as a client begins to settle, while longer appointments can lead to vocal strain and fatigue. Just as crucially, every client works with the same therapist across their entire block of therapy. You will never arrive to find an unfamiliar clinician who has to skim through historical case notes. Your therapist gets to know your subtle hesitations, your genuine interests, and the exact communication hurdles you encounter during the week. This consistency fosters deep trust, eliminating the anxiety of repeatedly explaining your difficulties and enabling steady, meaningful progress.',
	'k20f457ee' => 'Mateo Lindqvist',
	'k23beb0dc' => 'Written plan',
	'k271c1e00' => 'Many private health insurance providers cover speech and language therapy, though individual policy terms and reimbursement rates vary. Hibiki Speech provides itemised receipts following every session or block payment, containing all necessary diagnostic descriptions, service codes, and therapist registration numbers required by insurance assessors. We recommend contacting your insurance provider prior to your first assessment to confirm your specific coverage allowance. Our family coordinator Claire Dumont is experienced in preparing documentation that complies with insurer requirements.',
	'k28745744' => 'Every therapeutic journey at Hibiki Speech begins with careful, patient listening. Before opening assessment kits, formal testing booklets, or diagnostic charts, we observe how a person communicates naturally when completely at ease. We watch how a toddler explores toys on the mat, how a parent phrases everyday questions, or how an adult recovering from illness searches for words over a cup of tea. Communication is deeply personal, influenced by emotion, fatigue, and environmental comfort. By observing speech without judgment or immediate correction, your therapist identifies authentic communication strengths and pinpoints the precise moments where words become blocked or strained. This foundational stage ensures our subsequent therapy plan targets functional, real-world communication rather than artificial clinic exercises.',
	'k28d04c2c' => 'Monday to Friday',
	'k29a99298' => 'Assessment',
	'k2aa14202' => 'BOOKING',
	'k2b0032b1' => 'The five parts',
	'k2b11b931' => 'Hibiki Speech is located at 2F, 18 Linden Row, Westmere. Our clinic is situated in a quiet, accessible neighbourhood with excellent public transport links. A local tram line stops just a short walk from our front entrance on Linden Row. The building features complete step-free access from the street, with an automatic entrance and a modern lift providing easy access to our second-floor rooms for pushchairs and wheelchair users. If you are travelling by car, public pay-and-display parking is available along Linden Row and adjacent side streets. Inside our quiet clinic, you will find a comfortable, light-filled reception area where you can relax before your scheduled appointment.',
	'k2b5db239' => 'Founder, speech and language therapist',
	'k2d5cd99e' => 'Sunday and public holidays',
	'k2dae30a9' => 'Stammering in teenagers and adults',
	'k2e7d24dc' => 'Preparing for your initial assessment at 18 Linden Row is straightforward and stress-free. We suggest wearing comfortable, relaxed clothing suitable for sitting on floor mats or at low tables. If you are bringing a child, please feel free to bring their favourite cuddly toy, a familiar picture book, or a comfort item that helps them feel secure in new surroundings. For adult clients, bringing personal reading materials, a family photograph album, or a notebook of daily communication situations can be exceptionally useful. If you have previous medical summaries, audiology reports, or notes from school teachers or neurologists, please bring copies along. Most importantly, bring your questions and everyday observations; real-life examples are our most valuable diagnostic guide.',
	'k2f652f51' => 'We watch how each person talks when they are completely at ease before beginning any formal evaluation. Taking time to listen first helps us understand their natural rhythm and real communication needs.',
	'k324203aa' => 'Stammering in adults and teenagers',
	'k33eb3492' => '45 min',
	'k3458ac28' => 'Living with a stammer often shapes how people navigate education, social gatherings, and professional careers. Therapist Amara Osei works with teenagers and adults to demystify stammering, reduce physical struggle, and cultivate ease when speaking in demanding situations. Therapy does not chase artificial fluency or demand constant monitoring. Instead, Amara helps clients soften speech blocks, reduce avoidance behaviours, and manage situational anxiety during presentations, phone calls, and interviews. By practicing techniques in our calm clinic rooms and gradually extending them into real-world settings, clients develop genuine agency over their communication. The ultimate goal is speaking openly and authentic self-expression, allowing your personality and expertise to take centre stage without fear holding you back.',
	'k348fc024' => 'Can speech therapy sessions take place by video?',
	'k35c061ea' => 'Experiencing a stroke can abruptly sever access to familiar words, leaving intelligent, capable adults struggling to express basic thoughts, read books, or converse with family. Therapist Mateo Lindqvist works with clients navigating aphasia and acquired word-finding challenges. Sitting at a quiet window table overlooking Linden Row, therapy focuses on functional communication rather than abstract exercises. Mateo uses meaningful personal materials, such as family photo albums, favourite recipes, and relevant news articles, to rebuild semantic pathways and establish dependable retrieval strategies. We also introduce supportive communication techniques that family members can practice at home. Progress is measured by practical daily victories: ordering coffee independently, sharing stories with grandchildren on Sundays, or joining family dinner conversations with renewed ease and self-assurance.',
	'k35d69a98' => 'Navigating healthcare coverage should be simple and stress-free. Hibiki Speech provides itemised receipts for your insurer following every session or block payment, clearly detailing clinical service codes, therapist registration details, and appointment dates. While coverage levels vary across private health insurance policies, many providers reimburse speech and language therapy expenses when accompanied by our formal reports. Regarding scheduling, we ask that clients please give 24 hours\' notice to cancel or reschedule an appointment. Because our therapists reserve forty-five minutes exclusively for you, cancellations made with less than twenty-four hours\' notice may be billed at the standard session fee. This policy protects our clinical diary and helps us uphold our two-week waiting time commitment.',
	'k3601146c' => 'Price',
	'k38e39dfa' => 'New clients are seen within 2 weeks of the first call.',
	'k3b81923b' => 'Yes, we offer secure video therapy sessions for adult clients and home practice reviews. Video consultations are particularly convenient for adults with mobility limitations, busy professional schedules, or those living further from our Westmere clinic. Each video session lasts forty-five minutes and follows the identical therapeutic standard as our in-person appointments. We also provide thirty-minute video home practice reviews for parents who want quick clinical feedback on their child\'s home practice card without travelling to the clinic.',
	'k3c4259cc' => 'Following your assessment, therapy proceeds in a structured block of eight sessions, scheduled weekly for forty-five minutes each at €85 per session or €640 for the full block. You work exclusively with the same clinician throughout, providing unbroken therapeutic continuity and trust. After completing the eighth session, we pause for a comprehensive review. Together with your therapist, you evaluate progress against the goals established in your written plan. At this juncture, you decide whether to continue with another block of therapy, pause to consolidate gains independently with your home practice card, or successfully conclude therapy. We never lock clients into indefinite contracts; our care is always accountable, focused, and aligned with your real communication needs.',
	'k3cbe8173' => '30 min',
	'k3d308c02' => 'Mina provides voice care for teachers, singers, and professionals who speak throughout the day. She uses mirror exercises and vocal projection techniques to relieve strain and prevent hoarseness.',
	'k3e8e469a' => 'We maintain a straightforward, fixed pricing structure across all services, quoted in Euros without hidden extras. A first call with the family coordinator lasts 15 minutes and is completely Free. A comprehensive first assessment with written report takes 90 minutes and costs €180. An individual therapy session lasts 45 minutes and is priced at €85. For ongoing care, a block of 8 sessions of 45 minutes each is €640, providing structured weekly support. A home practice review, conducted at the clinic or via video, lasts 30 minutes and costs €45. For professional voice users, our structured voice care course comprises 6 sessions of 45 minutes each for €480. Finally, a school or workplace visit lasts 60 minutes and is €120.',
	'k3f1c0436' => 'Come and see the room.',
	'k3f278554' => 'We never expect young children to sit still at a formal desk. At Hibiki Speech, pediatric sessions take place on our floor mat and around low oak tables. Movement is a natural part of communication for young children. Our therapists integrate movement into language games, whether that means blowing feathers across a table, crawling to retrieve picture cards, or stacking wooden blocks. If a child needs a sensory pause or water break, we adjust the pace immediately without pressure.',
	'k40aa865d' => 'sessions per block',
	'k4181a89a' => 'Adult clients can choose between attending in-person sessions at our Westmere clinic or booking secure video consultations from the comfort of their home or workplace. In-person therapy takes place in our quiet, step-free rooms at 18 Linden Row, providing a peaceful retreat dedicated entirely to your rehabilitation. For clients with limited mobility, fatigue, or busy professional schedules, our video therapy sessions offer the identical forty-five-minute standard of personal care. Using screen-sharing tools and live exercises, your therapist guides your practice with identical attentiveness. Many adult clients choose a hybrid model, beginning with clinic visits for their initial assessment and later completing regular home practice reviews or therapy sessions online as their confidence and independence steadily grow.',
	'k44a044c2' => 'How quickly can we start therapy after contacting you?',
	'k44c3c180' => 'FEES',
	'k451c9d10' => 'CLINIC',
	'k457dd551' => 'Review',
	'k45fd21b9' => 'The room',
	'k4782b524' => 'Every voice finds its words at its own pace.',
	'k479030b6' => 'Voice care for professionals',
	'k47cc8329' => 'Early language and childhood communication',
	'k48552df6' => 'Block of 8 sessions',
	'k485a3432' => 'Reading aloud',
	'k4871da05' => 'How sessions work',
	'k495e41d1' => 'When communication becomes an effort, everyday routines at home, school, or work can feel exhausting. Whether words are slow to emerge in childhood or suddenly disrupted in adulthood, recognising the difficulty is the first step toward finding relief.',
	'k497146dd' => 'Margaret, 68: words returning after a stroke',
	'k4a904962' => '© 2014–2026 Hibiki Speech. The clinic, its people and prices are fictional.',
	'k4b28083a' => 'Our therapy rooms are intentionally peaceful and uncluttered, filled with morning light from large windows looking onto Linden Row. Rather than sterile examination suites, we have created warm, domestic environments finished in light oak and soft neutral tones. For our youngest visitors, low wooden tables and comfortable floor mats allow therapy to take place at eye level through play. Adults sit comfortably at window-side tables where conversation feels natural, with tea close at hand and space for personal reading materials. A mirror wall is tucked discreetly into one room to help clients observe vocal posture and mouth shapes without feeling self-conscious. In the corner, a comfortable sofa lets parents observe their child with complete ease. Every corner of our clinic is arranged to remove pressure and make speech feel welcome.',
	'k4db3bed1' => 'Ines founded the clinic in 2014 and focuses on late talkers and early language in children aged two to six. She works with families at low oak tables using unhurried play and picture cards.',
	'k4fe10c87' => 'In 2014, speech and language therapist Ines Halvorsen founded Hibiki Speech at 18 Linden Row in Westmere. Having worked across hospital wards and busy community centres, she envisioned a calm, independent clinic where therapy would never feel rushed or clinical. She designed Hibiki Speech around a fundamental premise: communication develops best when people feel completely safe and unhurried. From our second-floor rooms, we welcome young children taking their first steps into spoken words, alongside adults regaining language after life-changing neurological events. Over the years, our clinic has grown into a collaborative team of seven professionals, yet our founding spirit remains unchanged. We do not use generic exercises or rigid worksheets. Instead, we listen closely to how each individual speaks in everyday moments, crafting personal support that fits naturally into family life, school, or daily work.',
	'k508b24f5' => 'Your two-year-old points instead of naming.',
