	'k6a7e7316' => 'Hours',
	'k6a957510' => 'School or workplace visit',
	'k6ca28bee' => 'Many young children know exactly what they wish to say, but certain consonant sounds remain tangled or unclear, making it difficult for listeners outside the home to understand them. Speech and language therapist Noor Haddad specializes in speech sound clarity and its direct connection to early reading and phonological awareness. In our sessions, children explore how sounds feel in the mouth, using tactile games, feathers, and gentle mirror observation to master tricky sounds. We systematically address substitutions, omissions, and articulation patterns, ensuring children gain intelligibility before classroom reading begins. Because clear speech sounds form the bedrock of early literacy, resolving these patterns early prevents frustration at school and helps children approach books, phonics, and classroom discussions with quiet confidence.',
	'k6cc006a6' => 'Seven people, one room at a time.',
	'k6ce3bdc3' => 'Questions',
	'k6d711be6' => '60 min',
	'k6ebe3161' => 'Speaking with Claire Dumont',
	'k7048a005' => 'hello@hibikispeech.example',
	'k705550f8' => 'Book an assessment',
	'k71f15d0d' => '2F, 18 Linden Row, Westmere<br>+00 31 4072 5180<br>hello@hibikispeech.example',
	'k747dd70a' => 'We ask that clients please give at least 24 hours\' notice to cancel or reschedule an appointment. Because our therapists reserve forty-five minutes exclusively for you and your family, cancellations made with less than twenty-four hours\' notice may be charged the full session fee. Providing timely notice allows us to offer the appointment slot to another client seeking care and helps us maintain our two-week waiting time commitment.',
	'k75be6ccc' => 'In Margaret\'s case, a sudden stroke at age sixty-eight left her with severe word-finding difficulties and aphasia, isolating her from the book clubs and family gatherings she once loved. Margaret completed two blocks of therapy with Mateo Lindqvist in our quiet window room. Rather than working through generic flashcards, Mateo used Margaret\'s personal family photograph album to stimulate recall, practicing names, locations, and personal anecdotes in a relaxed setting. They established calm retrieval routines for moments when words felt blocked. Gradually, Margaret regained confidence in her spoken expression. Today, she participates comfortably in family conversations and proudly reads her young grandchildren a story every Sunday afternoon without distress.',
	'k7745ba1d' => 'At the mirror',
	'k7766fdee' => 'Seven people in the building',
	'k77bd411e' => 'Real communication growth happens between clinic visits, embedded in the familiar rhythm of everyday life. At the conclusion of each session, your therapist prepares a simple ten-minute daily practice card. This is never a burdensome packet of homework or theoretical paperwork. Instead, it offers two or three focused, enjoyable activities that fit effortlessly into your existing routine, such as naming games during bath time, vocal warm-ups while making coffee, or word-finding exercises using a family album. By keeping daily home practice to just ten minutes, families and adult clients can maintain consistent daily engagement without overwhelm. This steady, bite-sized practice reinforces neural pathways, solidifies newly learned speech habits, and transforms clinic gains into durable everyday competence.',
	'k78711e2b' => 'Speech and language therapy for children and adults.',
	'k7ab5d0b5' => 'Your voice is gone by Friday.',
	'k7c16f89a' => 'About the clinic',
	'k7cd5301d' => 'Lasting progress happens in everyday life between appointments. We provide a straightforward 10-minute daily practice card so clients and families can easily reinforce new speech habits at home.',
	'k7ceda0e6' => 'The page may have moved. Start again from the home page.',
