	'k7e322971' => 'Autistic children, picture-based communication (AAC)',
	'k8064f7aa' => 'Every smooth experience at Hibiki Speech begins with our family coordinator, Claire Dumont. Claire is the welcoming voice on the phone when you first contact our clinic, conducting our free fifteen-minute introductory consultations and matching each client to the appropriate specialist therapist. She manages our clinic diary to uphold our promise that new clients are seen within two weeks of their initial call. In addition to scheduling, Claire handles billing and prepares itemised receipts formatted specifically for private health insurance reimbursement. Whether you need directions to our Linden Row rooms, assistance rescheduling an appointment, or clarification regarding session fees, Claire provides prompt, empathetic administrative care that lets families focus entirely on their therapy.',
	'k8209a0d1' => 'Speech and language therapy for children and adults. Unhurried 45-minute sessions, one therapist from start to finish.',
	'k826c191a' => 'weeks to a first assessment',
	'k84653e3a' => 'It is hard to watch someone search for a word.',
	'k864d846e' => 'Children from 2 · Adults · Westmere',
	'k884edcda' => 'A floor game',
	'k88736060' => 'Words that came easily before a stroke now hide.',
	'k887cb869' => 'Ines Halvorsen',
	'k88978efd' => 'Carry it home',
	'k89b39b2e' => 'Hibiki Speech has provided thoughtful speech and language therapy for children and adults in Westmere since 2014. We offer unhurried care where clients work with one dedicated therapist from their initial assessment through their entire block of therapy.',
	'k89ca14a5' => 'To schedule your free fifteen-minute introductory phone call or discuss therapy for you or your child, please contact our family coordinator, Claire Dumont. You can reach Claire directly by telephone at +00 31 4072 5180 or by sending an email to hello@hibikispeech.example. During your initial call, Claire will take time to understand your communication concerns, explain how our clinicians work, discuss fees and health insurance receipts, and arrange your initial ninety-minute assessment. We respond to all voicemail and email inquiries promptly during our standard weekday hours, ensuring you receive clear guidance without delay.',
	'k8a9ca71f' => 'Stammering and picture-based communication',
	'k8b705118' => 'Saturday',
	'k8b8450e8' => 'Lukas works with autistic children, introducing picture-based communication systems (AAC) to foster clear everyday interactions. He partners closely with parents to integrate visual routines into home routines.',
	'k8ba2cf04' => 'Which languages do you support in therapy?',
	'k8c08a35d' => 'Every communication journey unfolds at its own pace, shaped by personal courage and consistent, gentle practice. Here are four short stories from our clinic showing how individualized speech therapy supported meaningful change in daily life.',
	'k8cadd7ed' => 'Mateo supports adults recovering from stroke, specializing in word-finding difficulties and rehabilitation after aphasia. He structures sessions around personal photo albums and everyday communication.',
	'k8d6fee90' => 'When assessing bilingual children, our therapists look at the child\'s total language capability across both languages rather than testing one language in isolation. A toddler who knows words across two languages often has a total vocabulary matching or exceeding monolingual milestones. We help parents understand how code-switching and sound development operate in multilingual homes, providing strategies that enrich language exposure without confusing the child. We never advise parents to drop their heritage language; authentic home communication is essential for healthy linguistic growth.',
	'k9402909e' => 'No, you do not need a medical referral from a doctor or paediatrician to book an appointment at Hibiki Speech. We welcome self-referrals directly from families, adult clients, and carers. You can contact our family coordinator Claire Dumont by phone or email to schedule a free fifteen-minute introductory call. However, if your doctor, neurologist, or school teacher has prepared a previous diagnostic report or medical summary, bringing a copy to your initial ninety-minute assessment can provide helpful background context for your therapist.',
	'k95a3918a' => 'At Hibiki Speech, we help children from age two discover clear, confident ways to communicate through play and gentle practice. Our clinic offers an unhurried setting where children feel safe to explore sounds, words, and social interaction.',
	'k95c66b91' => 'What is your cancellation policy?',
	'k960921f0' => 'Beginning speech therapy is a positive, supportive step, and we ensure the process is clear, transparent, and unhurried from the very start. From your initial free phone call through your comprehensive assessment and therapy block, you are guided every step of the way.',
	'k99e869ca' => 'When a child experiences moments of stammering, our aim is to reduce tension, foster easy communication, and preserve their natural joy in speaking. We help families understand how to soften communication pressures at home and school, providing children with calming strategies when words feel momentarily stuck. For autistic children and youngsters with limited verbal speech, therapist Lukas Brandt introduces augmentative and alternative communication (AAC), including structured picture-based systems. We introduce clear picture cards that allow children to make choices, share spontaneous comments, and express feelings without frustration. By establishing a reliable functional communication method, children gain practical agency in their everyday environments, which frequently opens new pathways toward verbal expression while immediately reducing communication-related distress.',
	'k9ad480f4' => 'Claire Dumont',
	'k9c144d61' => 'Voice care for teachers, singers, and daily speakers',
	'k9db26566' => 'A collaborative review after session 8 to decide whether to continue, pause, or finish.',
	'k9e4fae5e' => 'An initial assessment is an extensive ninety-minute session priced at €180, dedicated to evaluating medical background, speech sound articulation, language comprehension, and vocal patterns. It includes a comprehensive written report delivered within five working days outlining personalized therapy goals. Regular therapy sessions, by contrast, last forty-five minutes and cost €85 each (or €640 for a block of eight), focusing entirely on active practice, skill development, and home routines.',
	'ka00d45cc' => 'What is the difference between an assessment and a therapy session?',
	'ka1ecc725' => 'Sami, 15: stepping up to speak',
	'ka20d06f9' => 'A comprehensive 90-minute evaluation at the clinic, scheduled within 2 weeks of your call.',
	'ka2e66b4e' => 'A card deck with a parent on the sofa.',
	'ka43db570' => 'Our clinic is open Monday through Friday from 08:30 to 18:30, and on Saturday from 09:00 to 13:00. We are closed on Sundays and public holidays. All visits, including initial assessments and therapy sessions, are arranged by prior appointment to ensure each client receives private, unhurried care. Under our clinic promise, new clients are offered an initial assessment within two weeks of their first contact. We offer early morning and late afternoon appointment slots to accommodate school schedules and working commitments. Please note that session cancellations require at least 24 hours\' notice.',
