	'ka9c4b6c9' => 'Sessions',
	'kaa47b01a' => 'Sami, 15 — stammer',
	'kaabe9cfe' => 'A floor game with animal cards.',
	'kabde24b4' => 'Complete fee schedule',
	'kac40d082' => 'Fees and receipts',
	'kaca59ca0' => 'Do I need a doctor\'s referral to book an appointment?',
	'kad284bdc' => 'What happens if my child cannot sit still for forty-five minutes?',
	'kaf8740f3' => 'Hibiki Speech supports adults facing changes in communication, whether recovering from a stroke, living with a stammer, or experiencing vocal strain. We provide dignified, evidence-based therapy tailored to your personal goals and daily routines.',
	'kafcd75d5' => 'In Elena\'s case, teaching high school English left her voice strained, scratchy, and practically gone by Friday afternoon. At thirty-four, chronic vocal fatigue threatened her career and caused constant physical discomfort in her throat. Elena enrolled in our six-session voice care course with Mina Castell. Using our clinic mirror wall, Mina helped Elena recognize upper-chest tension and taught her diaphragmatic breathing exercises, humming drills, and semi-occluded vocal tract routines. Elena discovered how to project her voice effortlessly across a noisy classroom by using facial resonance rather than throat pressure. With these sustainable vocal habits in place, Elena now finishes her teaching week with complete vocal clarity, comfort, and vitality.',
	'kb063ef55' => 'A low table, a mirror wall, a mat.',
	'kb07cc3ad' => 'A clear summary report and therapy outline delivered within 5 working days.',
	'kb214a171' => 'Leo, 4: finding first sentences',
	'kb24ce0cd' => 'Free',
	'kb274857a' => 'Speech sounds and early literacy',
	'kb5410605' => 'Sessions at the clinic or by video',
	'kb645da9d' => 'At Hibiki Speech, we offer a calm, unhurried space where children and adults can build speech confidence without feeling rushed. Founded in 2014 by Ines Halvorsen, our clinic is arranged at floor and table level with natural light, low oak tables, and open room to think. We believe that communication develops best when people feel completely at ease.',
	'kb8aaa119' => 'Home practice review (clinic or video)',
	'kb96b0d7a' => 'Experiencing hoarseness by Friday afternoons, Elena completed a six-session voice care course with Mina, learning how to project comfortably in a noisy classroom.',
	'kbbaab4d9' => 'Between appointments, we ask clients and families to complete ten minutes of daily practice using the custom practice card provided at the end of each session. Ten minutes is specifically chosen to fit seamlessly into everyday domestic routines without creating stress or fatigue. Whether sorting picture cards during breakfast or practicing vocal resonance exercises while commuting, these short daily moments reinforce clinic progress and accelerate communication growth.',
	'kbbaff128' => 'Contact',
	'kbdd12cf8' => 'At Hibiki Speech, we believe in complete financial clarity with transparent, fixed pricing for all our clinical services. We provide itemised receipts for health insurance reimbursement and never charge hidden assessment or administrative costs.',
	'kbe9d7e92' => 'Who we see at Hibiki Speech',
	'kbf68ca19' => 'After an initial assessment and an eight-session block with Ines, Leo used simple picture-card routines to begin asking for things in short sentences at nursery.',
	'kbfbf8295' => 'Lukas Brandt',
	'kc1122046' => 'WHEN WORDS GET STUCK',
	'kc17e852f' => 'Late talkers and early language',
	'kc3755e61' => 'Call',
	'kc38f3967' => 'In Sami\'s case, a persistent stammer made secondary school presentations feel terrifying. At fifteen, he avoided raising his hand in class and dreaded oral assignments, fearing mockery from his peers. Sami worked through an eight-session therapy block with Amara Osei. Together, they explored how his vocal tract responded to anxiety, practicing speech modification techniques, pausing strategies, and gentle vocal onsets. Amara had Sami practice giving short talks in the safety of our clinic room, gradually building resilience and communicative ease. When his school term required an oral presentation, Sami declined the option of a written substitute and chose to give his history talk in person, speaking clearly and with immense personal pride.',
	'kc4e2ad72' => 'Read the stories',
	'kc51ab337' => 'We welcome both children and adults. For young families, we support toddlers from age two who are late to talk, school-age children working through speech sound difficulties, young people who stammer, and autistic children learning picture-based communication systems. For adults, our practice focuses on rehabilitation following a stroke, navigating word-finding difficulties and aphasia, alongside stammering management and vocal care for professional voice users such as teachers and performers. Whether speech has suddenly vanished following a medical emergency or has been an ongoing hurdle since early childhood, we provide compassionate, skilled guidance. We work collaboratively with families, carers, and educators, ensuring that communication gains made during clinic sessions translate seamlessly into the noisy, practical realities of homes, classrooms, and workplaces.',
	'kc62b028d' => 'Aphasia and word-finding after stroke',
	'kc6aeabf3' => 'Rather than cycling through rotating staff, each client works with one dedicated therapist from their first appointment through their complete block of sessions. Whether supporting a toddler finding their first words or an adult rebuilding speech after a stroke, we listen carefully before practice begins.',
	'kc851ba44' => 'Therapy session',
	'kcb0129c7' => 'minutes per session',
	'kcc7a915e' => 'Voice care course',
	'kcd4b0ee8' => 'Naming practice with a picture book.',
	'kce67d353' => 'Assessment at the low table.',
	'kce6802b4' => 'Listen',
	'kceefec2a' => 'Every 45-minute session is led by the same dedicated therapist, using practical games, mirror exercises, and real tasks. We work without rushing, ensuring that every exercise feels purposeful and unhurried.',
	'kcf1d2391' => 'Our primary language of assessment and therapy at our Westmere clinic is English. However, we have extensive clinical experience working with multilingual children and bilingual families. We evaluate speech sound development and language acquisition with careful consideration of a child\'s complete linguistic background, ensuring normal bilingual patterns are never misdiagnosed as developmental delays. When working with multilingual households, we encourage parents to speak their natural home language during domestic routines, as strong native language foundations support overall communication skills.',
	'kcf750b71' => 'Mon–Fri 08:30–18:30<br>Sat 09:00–13:00<br>Closed Sun and public holidays',
	'kd1813ed1' => 'Notes from the clinic',
	'kd327f15c' => 'Gradually, Margaret rebuilt her fluency and confidence in finding the right words. Today, she participates easily in family conversations and enjoys reading bedtime stories aloud to her grandchildren every Sunday.',
	'kd4d387f1' => 'Meet the team →',
	'kd5882b88' => 'Noor assists school-age children with speech sounds and articulation, linking spoken speech directly to early reading skills. She uses floor games and illustrated cards to reinforce clear pronunciation.',
	'kd6757cae' => 'Our pediatric clinicians provide compassionate care for our youngest communicators and their families. Founder Ines Halvorsen is a speech and language therapist specializing in late talkers and early language acquisition for children aged two to six, helping toddlers build functional spoken vocabulary through play. Therapist Lukas Brandt focuses on autistic children and picture-based communication, designing structured augmentative and alternative communication (AAC) frameworks that give non-speaking children reliable tools to express desires and connect with their world. Therapist Noor Haddad concentrates on speech sound development and its vital links to school-age reading and early literacy, helping children resolve articulatory substitutions so they approach classroom learning with confidence. Each therapist works directly with parents, turning clinical techniques into joyful everyday home interactions.',
	'kd699bee4' => 'Elena, 34 — teacher',
	'kd758ed44' => 'Adults after stroke (aphasia), word-finding',
	'kd827efed' => 'We welcome your inquiries and look forward to meeting you at our Westmere clinic. Whether you wish to book an assessment or simply ask an initial question, our family coordinator is here to help.',
	'kd85e167c' => 'Founded in 2014 by Ines Halvorsen',
	'kd8bb7521' => 'Your journey starts with a free fifteen-minute telephone conversation with our family coordinator, Claire Dumont. Claire listens to your concerns, answers initial questions about our Westmere clinic, and books your comprehensive assessment. We promise that all new clients are seen within two weeks of that initial call. The first assessment is an in-depth ninety-minute appointment with your designated speech and language therapist, costing €180. During this session, the therapist explores developmental background or medical history, observes natural speech, and conducts gentle diagnostic activities. Within five working days following the assessment, you receive a detailed written plan. This document outlines objective findings, explains speech mechanisms clearly, and proposes precise, practical therapy goals tailored to your individual daily life.',
	'kd930c8af' => 'Insurance receipts and cancellation policy',
	'kd930d5a7' => 'At the kitchen table',
	'kd976e856' => 'WHO SITS IN THE ROOM',
	'kd9c0094c' => 'Speech and language therapist',
	'kd9ea7d68' => 'Parents often wonder whether to seek advice or wait. It is worth scheduling a free fifteen-minute call with our coordinator Claire Dumont if your two-year-old has fewer than twenty words, if your child is understood by family but struggles at nursery, or if speaking causes visible distress or physical tension. When you bring your child to our Westmere clinic, you will never be asked to wait outside in a corridor. Parents sit comfortably in the room on our sofa or directly on the mat beside their child. You observe every interaction, see exactly how the therapist prompts each sound, and discover how ordinary playtime can become rich language practice without adding stress to your family routine.',
	'kdc21a3e7' => 'Take your time',
	'kdd841e8a' => 'A humming exercise with a hand on the chest.',
	'kde64d3c2' => 'Clear prices, receipts for your insurer.',
	'kdebfcd87' => 'From first call to your written plan',
	'kdee9e6e8' => 'Mina Castell',
	'kdfd94769' => 'Amara works with teenagers and adults who stammer, helping them build practical speaking strategies for daily life. Her sessions focus on school presentations, workplace discussions, and confident pacing.',
	'ke1157a57' => 'Weekly 45-minute therapy sessions with the same dedicated therapist throughout.',
	'ke4173394' => 'Clinic coordination and family support',
	'ke495c735' => 'In Leo\'s case, words were slow to arrive. At age four, he pointed at objects, pulled his parents\' sleeves, and became visibly frustrated when his nursery classmates could not understand his wishes. Following an initial assessment with Ines Halvorsen, Leo began a structured block of eight therapy sessions at our clinic. Ines introduced interactive floor games matching illustrated picture cards of animals and everyday toys, pairing physical play with clear verbal cues. At home, his parents carried out ten-minute daily games using picture cards on the sofa. By the conclusion of his therapy block, Leo was no longer relying on gestures; he began asking for things in short, clear sentences at nursery and happily engaging with peers.',
	'ke49c3a3f' => 'Family coordinator',
	'ke56f6d7e' => 'Our clinical framework is built around four dependable numbers that guide our practice: 45 minutes per therapy session, 8 sessions per structured block, 10 minutes of daily practice at home, and a commitment that new clients are seen within 2 weeks of their first call. We believe transparency in scheduling and structure brings peace of mind to families and adult clients. Forty-five minutes provides the optimum balance of energetic focus without cognitive fatigue. An eight-session block offers sufficient duration to achieve measurable clinical change while maintaining a clear endpoint for review. Ten minutes of daily practice ensures sustainable progress without burdening domestic routines. Finally, seeing new clients within two weeks ensures that early concerns are addressed without stressful delays.',
	'ke655ad30' => 'the word.',
	'ke6931cce' => 'Mouth shapes, side by side.',
	'kea287be5' => 'Call +00 31 4072 5180',
	'kea4c0208' => 'Teachers, lecturers, singers, and corporate professionals rely on their voices throughout long working days, but persistent vocal demands often lead to hoarseness, throat pain, or vocal loss by Friday afternoon. Therapist Mina Castell leads our dedicated voice care course, designed to restore healthy, sustainable vocal production. Working beside our clinic mirror wall, Mina evaluates vocal posture, breathing dynamics, and pitch resonance, identifying inefficient tension patterns in the neck and shoulders. Clients learn practical vocal warm-ups, semi-occluded vocal tract exercises, and resonance techniques that allow them to project clearly across noisy classrooms or meeting rooms without straining delicate vocal folds. We equip you with immediate vocal preservation tools that protect your livelihood and keep your voice clear and reliable all week long.',
	'keae038b7' => 'The numbers behind our care',
	'ked8968b4' => 'Noor Haddad',
	'kedd5623a' => 'When you arrive at our second-floor clinic, Claire Dumont welcomes you into our quiet waiting area with a cup of tea or a picture book. There are no clinical smells, buzzer systems, or intimidating diagnostic machinery. For children, the assessment feels like an enjoyable playdate: they explore toy sets and picture cards on our floor mat alongside their parents, taking breaks whenever needed. For adult clients, the session takes place at a peaceful oak table bathed in window light. Your therapist chats comfortably with you about your daily communication experiences, taking notes and guiding gentle exercises at your pace. We ensure you leave feeling heard, fully informed, and confident about the path ahead.',
	'kefe96bfe' => 'Margaret, 68 — word-finding after a stroke',
	'kf1735c64' => 'In Margaret\'s case, routine conversations had become hesitant after a stroke, leaving familiar words just out of reach. Over two blocks of therapy with Mateo Lindqvist, she practiced naming strategies using personal photographs from her family album rather than generic exercises, working in a calm setting at her own pace.',
	'kf1c35e58' => 'Through an eight-session block with Amara, Sami practiced speech techniques for classroom presentations and chose to deliver his history talk independently.',
	'kf1f5e96f' => 'Amara Osei',
	'kf28f8f46' => 'New clients seen within 2 weeks',
	'kf2a8ba2c' => 'Carry it home: the ten-minute daily practice card',
	'kf2c71784' => 'Children develop speech at their own individual tempo, but when a two-year-old relies solely on pointing or pulling hands rather than using spoken words, gentle early support can make an enormous difference. Led by our founder Ines Halvorsen, our early language sessions use playful, child-led activities around low oak tables and floor mats. We do not test children at desks or demand repetitive drills. Instead, we follow what captures their imagination, whether that means rolling a toy train, sorting animal cards, or stacking building blocks. By pairing engaging play with targeted language models, we help toddlers connect sounds to meaningful daily desires. Parents participate actively in every session, learning how to create low-pressure conversational routines at home that encourage two-word combinations and everyday vocabulary.',
	'kf3556e8f' => 'Hibiki Speech brings together seven dedicated professionals who share a deep commitment to calm, individualized speech and language therapy. Working collaboratively from our Westmere clinic, each team member brings focused expertise to children, adults, and families.',
	'kf4c6f851' => 'Notes',
	'kf624e0e9' => 'How do you work with bilingual children?',
	'kf7f4395f' => 'Leo, 4 — late talker',
	'kf82c912f' => 'Practise',
	'kf8511c13' => 'Late talkers and early language (ages 2–6)',
	'kf9741675' => 'Practice at home',
	'kf97a1b6f' => 'At Hibiki Speech, care is personal and continuous. You work with one dedicated practitioner throughout your entire block of therapy, supported by a close team sharing insights across child development, neurological rehabilitation, and voice care.',
	'kfa2a5a06' => 'Elena, 34: keeping a clear voice through Friday',
	'kfa733024' => 'Quiet rooms designed for listening',
	'kfc206df9' => 'First visit',
	'kfd7c116f' => 'A stammer is making class presentations dreadful.',
